<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n2156" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ambĭ-fārĭus</span></b> ,
			a, um, adj.
		cf. the Gr. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δι-φάσιος,
			τρι-φάσιος</span>, and v. aliquot-fariam, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>that has two
			sides</i>, <i>of double meaning</i>, <i>ambiguous</i> (only post-class.): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">fabulae,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Arn. p. 181</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">obtentio,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. p. 182</span></i>
			.—Hence, </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>1.</b> * <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ambĭfārĭē</span></b> ,
				adv., <i>ambiguously</i>,
					<i><span class="en">Mamert. Stat. Anim. 1,
			3</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ambĭfārĭ-am</span></b> ,
			adv. (orig. <i>acc. fem.</i> sc. partem),
				<i>on two sides</i>, <i>in two
			ways</i>, <i>ambiguously</i>, = in utramque partem,
					<i><span class="en">App. Flor. 4, 18, p. 360, 25</span></i>;
			so <i><span class="en">id. Mag. p. 276, 2</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
    <div class="alpheios-lex-alph-source">From <u>
            <u>A Latin Dictionary</u>
        </u> (Charlton T. Lewis, Charles Short, Oxford, Clarendon Press, 1879) </div>
</div>